window.docContents[195].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.SignalSession.CliBinaryPq/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___SignalSession___CliBinaryPq":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession › CliBinaryPq.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the symbolic proof 4 headline theorems depend on it 482 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (46)abbrev libsignalSessionLibabbrev lsRustNoAllocShimSymCliabbrev lsRustAllocSymCliabbrev lsRustDeallocSymCliabbrev lsRustReallocSymCliabbrev lsRustAllocZeroedSymCliabbrev lsReadFileSymabbrev lsWriteFileSymabbrev lsReadStdinSymabbrev lsWriteStdoutSymabbrev lsMemrchrSymabbrev lsFromUtf8Symabbrev lsFmtWriteSymabbrev lsFormatInnerSymabbrev lsDurationSinceSymabbrev lsTimeAddSymabbrev lsBlackBoxSymabbrev lsCompress256Symabbrev lsAesEncSymabbrev lsAesDecSymabbrev lsPubFromSecretSymabbrev lsDiffieHellmanSymabbrev lsStaticSecretDropSymabbrev lsSharedSecretDropSymdef cliDehookedSymsPlaceddef cliPqxdhHookTablePlaceddef cliHookTablePlaceddef cliPanicSymbolsPlaceddef isCliPanicSymbolPlaceddef cliExternsPlaceddef cliExternsPlacedSigdef cliProgPlacedSigtheorem libsignalSessionLib_main_blockdef cliTokenPatchPlaceddef CliRunsToPlaceddef cliRunPlacedSigdef DirectOrBranchStubdef CliElfCodeMatchesPlaceddef CliPqxdhInputsdef CliReachesOOMPlaceddef OutcomeOrExcusedAbortdef CliSpecPqxdhOrExcusedAbortdef CliSpecPqxdhNoMatchOrExcusedAbortdef CliPqxdhElfCorrectPlaceddef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectPlacedAtdef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectPlaced\n\n\n\nWhole-process correctness of the libsignal-cli ELF (PQXDH mode)Trusted: the statement. Read it in full (see Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md). CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectPlaced bytes states that for every pair of placements (mpl, mmpl) linked at bytes (libsignalSessionLib.LinkedAt bytes mpl, VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib.LinkedAt bytes mmpl), bytes parses as an ElfImage matching both libraries (Placed.CliElfCodeMatchesPlaced mpl mmpl elf), and for all hooks W : CliHooks and model extras X : UnreachedPqxdhPrimitives, the process Placed.cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl elf W (after Placed.cliTokenPatchPlaced, DEV-CLI10) is total except on .OutOfMemory (CliReachesOOMPlaced, DEV-CLI15) and satisfies CliSpecPqxdh (PqDir.lean) and CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch (PqDirNoMatch.lean, DEV-CLI11) at ⟨W.C, W.Q⟩.Scope exclusions* keygen (PqDir.lean) and usage-error paths (CliRejectsMalformedCommandLine).* Party states outside PqxdhPartyInSpecDomain; init when a session already exists (DEV-C-PREV); non-canonical pre-key messages (DEV-CLI3); inputs of 2^32 bytes or more (2^32 - 2048 for a pre-key message's inner message).* After an accepted pre-key recv over a non-matching session: the written session file bytes and all subsequent calls on that directory (DEV-CLI11).* Outputs and files on runs that reach .OutOfMemory (DEV-CLI15).* CPUs with AES or PMULL, and SPQR's CPU probe (Placed.cliTokenPatchPlaced, DEV-CLI10).Deviations of a run of the ELFDEV-M6 (machine model): fixed stack, heap, and mmap layout. Each valid pair of multi-block placements mpl (libsignalSessionLib.LinkedAt bytes mpl) and mmpl (VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib.LinkedAt bytes mmpl, Placed.CliElfCodeMatchesPlaced mpl mmpl elf) places code and data where elf maps them (for the pinned non-PIE ELF cliElfBytes, linked with stock ld.lld under cli-elf/stock.ld at load base 0x400000). The process gets an 8 MiB stack with its top at 0x7fff_ffff_0000 (DEV-CLI7), the engine's default auxiliary vector (AT_RANDOM = 16 zero bytes, AT_HWCAP = 0x3), mmap slots from 0x6000_0000_0000 (SignalSession/Process.lean), and brk starting at elf.brkStart. A real kernel places the stack, brk, and the mmap area at random addresses. Effect: out of scope: no claim for another stack/mmap/brk layout.DEV-M7 (machine model): this ELF and its build. The closed headline claims are about the ELF pinned by SHA-256 in CliElf.lean (cliElfBytes): libsignal v0.105.4's libsignal-cli CLI built from source by scripts/cli-elf-stock --stdbin --build from third_party/libsignal/libsignal-session/cli-elf/stock/inputs_stock_stdbin.lock (rustc 1.98.1 and its aarch64-unknown-linux-musl self-contained/ CRT objects and libc.a, stock LLVM ld.lld 22.1.8 --no-relax under cli-elf/stock.ld, zig 0.16.0 for rdl_shim.S, std-main, and libsignal-session/translation.toml plus cli/io/translation.toml, with the software AES and SHA-2 backends). Effect: out of scope: production builds, other compilers and other flags are not covered.DEV-M11 (machine model): each call is a fresh process. Each init / send / recv in Placed.cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl elf W runs from loadState (after Placed.cliTokenPatchPlaced) to exit_group or SIGABRT, with constant clock UNIX_EPOCH. Effect: out of scope for long-lived processes.DEV-E1 (machine model): hooks write only their outputs. Under AAPCS64 a callee may clobber caller-saved registers (x0–x18, SIMD/FP, NZCV), whereas each hook in cliHookTablePlaced updates only its specified output registers/memory (cliBcmpHook writes x0; durationSinceExactHook writes its 24-byte result). Unhooked zero stubs halt and are forbidden by Placed.CliRunsToPlaced. Effect: w.l.o.g., argued for standard compiler code generation.DEV-E7 (machine model): the ELF aborts where the model panics. Protocol-model panics map to aborted, and the ELF's panic symbols (isCliPanicSymbolPlaced) terminate the process with SIGABRT (abortOnPanic, CliProcess.lean). Effect: availability only; none on confidentiality or integrity.\n\n\n\nRelocatable Obj.MultiPlacedLib (libsignalSessionLib) CLI Hook Table & Correctness\n\nabbrev libsignalSessionLibL93–95 ↗#The multi-block placed library libsignalSessionMultiLib (624 code blocks, 1,248 data objects, 4 exports) extracted from the .rlib/.o archives in GeneratedLean.LibsignalSessionPlacedObj.\n\nabbrev lsRustNoAllocShimSymCliL97–98 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsRustAllocSymCliL99 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsRustDeallocSymCliL100 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsRustReallocSymCliL101 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsRustAllocZeroedSymCliL102 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsReadFileSymL104 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsWriteFileSymL105 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsReadStdinSymL106 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsWriteStdoutSymL107 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsMemrchrSymL109 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsFromUtf8SymL110 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsFmtWriteSymL111 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsFormatInnerSymL112 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsDurationSinceSymL113–114 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsTimeAddSymL115–116 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsBlackBoxSymL117–118 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsCompress256SymL119 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsAesEncSymL120 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsAesDecSymL121 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsPubFromSecretSymL122–123 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsDiffieHellmanSymL124–125 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsStaticSecretDropSymL126–127 ↗#\n\nabbrev lsSharedSecretDropSymL128–129 ↗#\n\ndef cliDehookedSymsPlacedL131–146 ↗#The 9 extern symbols de-hooked so the linked ELF bytes execute. Stock ld.lld cutover: memcpy and memset, whose .symtab definitions in the stock link are VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib blocks 20 / 21. Earlier F3 + IO.6b allocator/IO cutover: 7 mangled symbols, the 5 Rust global-allocator symbols (rdl_shim.S → VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib) and read_file / read_stdin (libsignal_cli_io). (<String as Clone>::clone becomes an intra-library libsignalSessionLib block under SC-1 route (I).)\n\ndef cliPqxdhHookTablePlacedL148–185 ↗#Mangled-symbol PQXDH and SPQR primitive rows (18 rows) matching libsignalSessionMultiLib, with libcrux_hmac::hmac wired over shared mallocng at placement mmpl.\n\ndef cliHookTablePlacedL187–213 ↗#Mangled-symbol CLI hook table (37 rows) matching libsignalSessionMultiLib after the F3 + IO.6b allocator/IO cutover (5 __rust_* allocator rows, <String as Clone>::clone, read_file, and read_stdin removed so the linked ELF bytes execute; aes_256_cbc_{encrypt,decrypt} and libcrux_hmac::hmac wired over VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib at placement mmpl) and the stock ld.lld cutover (memset and memcpy removed: they run as mallocngLib blocks 21 / 20).\n\ndef cliPanicSymbolsPlacedL215–234 ↗#The 18 mangled panic extern symbols of libsignalSessionMultiLib mapped to Rust.panicked.\n\ndef isCliPanicSymbolPlacedL236–238 ↗#Canonical panic-symbol predicate for libsignalSessionLib.\n\ndef cliExternsPlacedL240–246 ↗#Mangled-symbol CLI extern map under Obj.MultiPlacedLib (libsignalSessionLib + mallocngLib placement mmpl).\n\ndef cliExternsPlacedSigL248–251 ↗#Mangled-symbol CLI extern map with .Panicked mapped to SIGABRT (abortOnPanic).\n\n\n\ndef cliProgPlacedSigL255–261 ↗#Relocatable program of a CLI run: block 617 of libsignalSessionLib under mpl with cliExternsPlacedSig mmpl W (whose extern table equals main's block's by libsignalSessionLib_main_block). Because Step fetches instructions from s.mem via Program.fetchMem whenever externAt? pc = none, unhooked calls execute the Perm.rx ELF bytes loaded by elf.loadState.\n\ntheorem libsignalSessionLib_main_blockL263–274 ↗#Kernel-checked guard that block 617 of libsignalSessionLib exists and shares the exact externs list of main's block (with main at offset 0), ensuring cliProgPlacedSig induces the same externAt? and Step relation as main's block without pinning main's block index.\n\ndef cliTokenPatchPlacedL276–280 ↗#Relocatable SPQR CPU-probe patch (STORAGE.0 := 0 at mpl.ρ tokenStorageName, TOKEN.state := 0 at mpl.ρ tokenName + 8; see cliTokenPatch, DEV-CLI10).\n\ndef CliRunsToPlacedL282–287 ↗#Relocatable CliRunsTo under multi-block placements (mpl, mmpl).\n\ndef cliRunPlacedSigL289–293 ↗#Relocatable cliRunAbortOnPanic under multi-block placements (mpl, mmpl).\n\ndef DirectOrBranchStubL295–303 ↗#External resolution stubVa = mpl.ρ sym reaches the .symtab definition targetVa in elf: either directly (stubVa = targetVa, stock ld.lld link) or via a 4-byte-aligned executable (Perm.rx) 1-word unconditional branch B targetVa at stubVa (--branch-stubs slot in .img.text).\n\ndef CliElfCodeMatchesPlacedL305–338 ↗#Relocatable CliElfCodeMatches under libsignalSessionLib placement mpl and VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib placement mmpl (SR-28 #3 and GK2 K2/K3):1. libsignalSessionLib placement, in-ELF match, and writable-data disjointness (mpl);2. VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib placement, in-ELF match, and writable-data disjointness (mmpl);3. K3(a): cross-library code-block and writable-data disjointness plus externAt? = none across all mallocngLib code bytes and at every de-hooked resolution mpl.ρ sym;4. K3(b): every sym ∈ cliDehookedSymsPlaced (the 9 external de-hooked symbols) resolves to a unique defined STT_FUNC .symtab entry targetVa in elf (DirectOrBranchStub elf (mpl.ρ sym) targetVa) with externAt? targetVa = none.\n\n\n\nThe PQXDH-mode input domain, and runs that reach .OutOfMemory\n\ndef CliPqxdhInputsL347–371 ↗#The inputs of the PQXDH-mode specs at model primitives W: the inputs of the calls of CliSpecPqxdh's five clauses and of CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch, for a party state st in the domain (PqxdhPartyInSpecDomain W st):1. init <peer> bundle with no session, any typed bundle b and the 192 coin bytes t;2. send <peer> of a plaintext m below 2^32 bytes with the 64 coin bytes r;3. recv <peer> of 2 ‖ c with c below 2^32 bytes;4. recv <peer> of 3 ‖ m.bytes for a typed pre-key message m whose inner message is below 2^32 - 2048 bytes, at any session state (no session, a matching one: CliSpecPqxdh; one that does not match: CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch);5. recv <peer> of any input c below 2^32 bytes whose first byte is neither 2 nor 3, or of nothing. In 2–5 the receive coins rc are any 32 bytes.\n\ndef CliReachesOOMPlacedL373–381 ↗#Run on i under (mpl, mmpl) and W reaches s.status = .OutOfMemory (brk / mmap / mprotect / mremap exhaustion) from Placed.cliTokenPatchPlaced mpl s0 (DEV-CLI10, DEV-CLI15). By determinism of Step, reaching .OutOfMemory forces Placed.cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl elf W i = none and excludes .Exception, .Halted, and divergence.\n\nSpecs total except .OutOfMemory (DEV-CLI15)\n\ndef OutcomeOrExcusedAbortL385–390 ↗#The outcome of run on i meets P, or run has no outcome on an excused input (DEV-CLI15: total except .OutOfMemory): either run i = some o with P o, or run i = none and exc i. With exc := fun _ => False it is equivalent to ∃ o, run i = some o ∧ P o, and with P := (· = e) it is equivalent to run i = some e.\n\ndef CliSpecPqxdhOrExcusedAbortL392–434 ↗#CliSpecPqxdh total except .OutOfMemory (DEV-CLI15). CliSpecPqxdh run X W (PqDir.lean) with each clause's conclusion run i = some e replaced by OutcomeOrExcusedAbort exc run i (· = e): on the clause's input i the run is total with exactly the clause's outcome, except when run i = none and i is excused (exc i). The five clauses are CliSpecPqxdh's (1. init, 2. send, 3. recv of 2 ‖ c, 4. recv of a typed pre-key message with no session or a matching one, 5. recv of any other first byte or of nothing), in the same order, with the same binders, hypotheses and outcomes, including the stdinCapBytes / maxPlaintextBytes rejections (DEV-CLI21). With exc := fun _ => False it is equivalent to CliSpecPqxdh run X W.\n\ndef CliSpecPqxdhNoMatchOrExcusedAbortL436–453 ↗#CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch total except .OutOfMemory (DEV-CLI15). CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch run X W (PqDirNoMatch.lean) with its conclusion ∃ o, run i = some o ∧ OutcomeMatchesModelExceptPath … replaced by OutcomeOrExcusedAbort exc run i …, with the same binders, hypotheses and outcomes, including the stdinCapBytes rejection (DEV-CLI21). With exc := fun _ => False it is equivalent to CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch run X W.\n\ndef CliPqxdhElfCorrectPlacedL455–466 ↗#Relocatable CliPqxdhElfCorrect under placements (mpl, mmpl), total except .OutOfMemory (DEV-CLI15). elf matches the placed code (Placed.CliElfCodeMatchesPlaced mpl mmpl elf), and for every choice of hooks W (no hypothesis on W) and every model extras X, the process Placed.cliRunPlacedSig mpl mmpl elf W is total and meets CliSpecPqxdh and CliSpecPqxdhNoMatch at ⟨W.C, W.Q⟩ except on inputs where the run reaches .OutOfMemory (CliReachesOOMPlaced mpl mmpl elf W).\n\ndef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectPlacedAtL468–471 ↗#Relocatable CliPqxdhBinaryCorrect at specific placements (mpl, mmpl).\n\ndef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectPlacedL473–483 ↗#Relocatable CliPqxdhBinaryCorrect: universally quantified over every pair of multi-block placements mpl (libsignalSessionLib.LinkedAt bytes mpl) and mmpl (VerifiedLibraries.mallocngLib.LinkedAt bytes mmpl).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliBinaryPq.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.SignalSession.CliBinaryPq/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___SignalSession___CliBinaryPq"}});